@yangzhe1991/dsh-web-enhance README · Features：- When **on** (default), every "Think" reasoning row is expanded automatically — including rows that mount while the agent is still streaming — so you read the full reasoning text without clicking each one.
  - Toggle it off to restore the built-in collapsed one-line summaries.
  - The preference persists across reloads (localStorage). Manually collapsing an individual row is respected and will not be force-expanded.

@yangzhe1991/dsh-web-enhance README · Features：- **Mutually exclusive with the ¥ meter**: the badge renders while the session's latest request runs on GLM (provider routes `zai-coding-cn` / `zai` / `zhipu`, or any model id starting with `glm`); switching back to DeepSeek restores the ¥ meter. The two gates never mix.
  - **Display**: a five-part compact badge like `5h额度18%，周额度35%，周窗口40%，安全线52%，5d15h后重置` (5h quota 18%, weekly quota 35%, week-window elapsed 40%, the fixed-overhead safety line at 52%, weekly reset in 5d15h). Comparing the weekly quota against the week window's time progress tells whether you are burning the week ahead of its clock. Hover adds each window's **time left until reset**, the safety-line math (reserve, headroom, an over-the-line warning), the plan tier and the data timestamp.
  - **Fixed-overhead safety line** — the line is `weekly quota − fixedDaily × days-until-reset`; usage above it means the reserved budget can no longer cover the fixed overhead even if everything else stops immediately. `fixedDaily` (credits/day) is a plugin config field, default **13000**; override it via the plugin row's `config: { fixedDaily: … }` in your profile's cordis patch. The

@yangzhe1991/dsh-web-enhance README · Features：- **Background**: GLM's sensitive-word review kills the streaming connection outright. The host (agent-loop) actually persists every chunk received before the cut as an `assistant/attempt` event — the data survives — but the stock web frontend treats that event type as invisible: the transient streaming rows are retired, no renderer claims the event, and the thinking/body on screen disappears together, leaving only an error row.
  - **What this plugin does**: registers a conversation node definition claiming `assistant/attempt` events, expands the compact stream records inside the event, reassembles the thinking/text blocks under the server's own "safe interrupted prefix" rules (tool calls are always dropped — they were never dispatched before the cut, and a call without a result would only mislead), and emits a view node of the **official `assistant-step` kind** so the stock renderer draws it: markdown body, thinking disclosures and the "Stopped" badge all behave exactly as usual.
  - **Both paths covered**: the moment of the cut (live settlement — retiring the transient rows and showing the kept row land in the same frame) and histor

